        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Does the ontology provide an additional &quot;external&quot; identifier, i.e., a guarantee globally unique and persistent identifier assigned by an accredited body? If yes, is the external identifier a DOI? This metric corresponds to the O&apos;FAIRe question F1Q2, which assesses FAIR principle F1. Its raw value is the number of credits obtained in the question, measured on an ordinal scale with the following levels: 0 (External identifier is absent); 3 (External identifier is present but invalid); 6 (External identifier is present and valid); 9 (External identifier is an invalid DOI); 11 (External identifier is a valid DOI).</obo:IAO_0000115>
